{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 3 may be the only input to the output node, so adding a conv there can rescue a disconnected cell (exp 6 vs 7-10, exp 1 vs 2-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 5 is also none can sever the output from the input, collapsing accuracy (exp 21, 29 vs 22, 30)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, fewer alternative paths reach node 3, so deleting edge 3 is far more damaging (exp 21, 29 vs 23, 28)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a new skip path into the output helps substantially, whereas replacing an existing conv on edge 5 with skip loses capacity (exp 45, 50 vs 46, 47, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a missing input-to-output edge into a skip adds a residual path, while replacing an existing op on edge 3 gives little or negative change (exp 81, 85 vs 82, 83, 86, 87)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is absent, adding a conv on edge 4 opens or strengthens the main path into the output (exp 91, 93 vs 92, 94)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "If node 2 receives no conv from node 1, a 3x3 conv on edge 5 adds more needed depth than when edge 2 already supplies a conv (exp 13 vs 14, 15 vs 16, 17 vs 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the direct input-output edge with an identity removes learnable capacity (exp 87, 90 vs 81, 85, 88)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv on the last edge for skip loses the strongest operation feeding the output (exp 43, 47, 49 vs 44, 45, 48, 50)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv between intermediate nodes with parameter-free pooling hurts more than replacing none, skip, or 1x1 conv (exp 54, 58, 59 vs 52, 55, 56)."}], "tok": 17437, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor